{title: Auld Lang Syne}
{artist: Robert Burns (1788)}
{key: G}

{start_of_verse: label="1."}
Should [G]auld acquaintance [D]be for[G]got,
and [G]never brought to [C]mind?
Should [G]auld acquaintance [D]be for[Emi]got,
and [C]auld [D]lang [G]syne?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
For [G]auld lang syne, my [D]dear,
for [G]auld lang [C]syne,
we'll [G]take a cup o' [D]kindness [Emi]yet,
for [C]auld [D]lang [G]syne.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: label="2."}
And [G]surely ye'll be [D]your pint-[G]stowp!
and [G]surely I'll be [C]mine!
And [G]we'll take a cup o' [D]kindness [Emi]yet,
for [C]auld [D]lang [G]syne.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
